{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take a census.</b> To arrange them so that they would enter the land immediately, each man under his banner, without war, but rather that the nations would clear out before them — as some of them did, as Scripture testified in saying (Isaiah 17:9), כַּעֲזוּבַת הַחֹרֶשׁ וְהָאָמִיר אֲשֶׁר עָזְבוּ מִפְּנֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל. Perhaps these were families of the Girgashite, concerning whom the Sages of blessed memory said that he rose up and cleared out from before them. But through the corruption of the spies, the seven nations grew worse for forty years, and it became necessary to put them under the ban." "<b>By the number of names.</b> For at that time every individual of that generation was reckoned by his name, which indicated his personal form, to their perfection — after the manner of וָאֶדָּעֲךָ בְשֵׁם (Exodus 33:17). This was not so for the generation that entered the land, and therefore they were not numbered by the number of names (Numbers 26:2), nor were any remembered except the heads of the families and the number of individuals. And with this He indicated that the intent was that those same individuals in person would live and inherit the land, and not one of them would be lost."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:32.763168072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}